WEBVTT

00:00:00.142 --> 00:00:03.202
Choosing a summary is a conceptual decision.

00:00:03.202 --> 00:00:07.167
Counts and proportions fit nominal categories naturally.

00:00:07.167 --> 00:00:09.562
Ordinal variables often support medians and percentiles.

00:00:09.562 --> 00:00:16.282
Numeric variables may use means and standard deviations when the mean is meaningful and the distribution is

00:00:16.282 --> 00:00:20.002
appropriate. Skewed numeric data often benefits from median and interquartile range.

00:00:20.002 --> 00:00:25.367
Do not apply the same summary mechanically to every column in a dataframe.

00:00:25.367 --> 00:00:29.317
Connect this idea to a hospital combining patient tables, device JSON, and clinical notes.

00:00:29.317 --> 00:00:33.532
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:33.532 --> 00:00:40.932
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:40.932 --> 00:00:45.297
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:45.297 --> 00:00:49.440
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
